# macOS title-bar clicks

On macOS, Jcat's title bar must not swallow clicks. This has regressed more than once: Settings, More, the language menu, Run, Compile, and the run-class menu stop opening.

Cause: `-webkit-app-region: drag` on `.titlebar` or on a parent of those controls. A `no-drag` child inside a drag parent is not enough. Transparent `no-drag` regions are ignored by macOS, so the click drags the window instead of reaching the button. DevTools and synthesized clicks can still fire and hide the bug. Only a real pointer click shows it.

Rules:

- `.titlebar` itself stays `no-drag`.
- Drag only empty regions: `.brand` and `.title-drag`. Never put drag on `.actions`, `.title-end`, or any element that contains a button, menu, or select.
- `.actions` and `.title-end` stay `no-drag` and use an opaque `background-color` (`var(--paper)`), not `transparent`.
- Every title-bar button, including Settings, must itself use an opaque `background-color`. A transparent button punches a hole in the parent no-drag region, and macOS treats that hole as window dragging. DevTools `elementFromPoint` and synthesized clicks still hit the button and hide this.
- A closing dialog must not leave `.modal-backdrop` on screen. While it is leaving (`is-out`), it has `pointer-events: none`.
- After any title-bar or dialog change, verify a real pointer click opens Settings. Do not treat a DevTools click as proof.
